<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caesar's Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/49-bce">49</a>–45 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Great Roman Civil War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caesar's Civil War was fought from 49 to 45 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and the conservative faction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>. It began when Caesar crossed the Rubicon into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in January 49 BCE; his victories at Pharsalus (48), Thapsus (46) and Munda (45) left him master of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and opened the way to the end of the Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war.jpg" alt="Caesar's Civil War" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Historicair, Ifly6 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Ancient_Rome_at_Caesar_time_(with_conquests)-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
